 "notes": "Single OCR'd Blue Ridge / Inner Piedmont map sheet; map face is OCR noise; description columns interleave with photo captions. Two cross sections (A-A', vertical exaggeration 4; B-B', no vertical exaggeration) of crystalline thrust sheets (Walhalla nappe, Jocassee thrust sheet) with faults and form lines, no drill holes; not traced from images, only names, exaggeration, datum and the legible label Hgn recorded. Faults named in the explanation abbreviations and text recorded; legend-only fault and fold types not recorded. The Brevard Imbricate Stack (BIS) is a structural stack, not recorded as a fault. Some symbols garbled ('Ean', '[bon'). Hatcher (2004) printed with OCR punctuation errors; corrected in the citation value. SUBSURFACE: crystalline sections with fault and form-line geometry only; no unit tops or bases.",
